      "file_path": "packages/core/src/safe-git.ts",
      "line_number": 10,
      "line_end": 14,
      "title": "safeGit return type changed but callers still expect a string",
      "description": "safeGit now resolves to a GitResult object instead of the stdout string. currentBranch in packages/cli/src/branch.ts:7 still calls name.trim(), and changedFiles in packages/cli/src/status.ts:6 still calls out.split(). In currentBranch, trim throws a TypeError, its catch swallows it, and it always returns null. The CLI in main.ts then always prints \"not a git repository\" and exits 1. Update currentBranch and changedFiles to read result.stdout in the same change. Another option is to keep a string-returning wrapper for existing callers.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "lens:return-shape-contract-break",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
