      "title": "Removed throw breaks callers that rely on git failures",
      "description": "safeGit now catches every git failure and returns a non-zero code instead of throwing. currentBranch in packages/cli/src/branch.ts:8 detects a missing repository only through that throw. If currentBranch reads stdout but not code, it returns an empty string outside a repository instead of null. main.ts then carries on, and changedFiles reports zero changes instead of an error. Make currentBranch and changedFiles check result.code and handle non-zero codes. For example, currentBranch should return null when the code is not 0.",
